  "notes": "Compound of ⟦{草|くさ}→草：02206_kusa⟧ (grass, weeds) + むしる (to pluck, pull out). Refers specifically to pulling weeds by hand.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {草|くさ}むしり⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to weed, to pull weeds\n- ⟦{庭|にわ}→庭：02239_niwa⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{草|くさ}むしり: garden weeding\n- {草|くさ}むしり⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{疲|つか}れる→疲れる：00901_tsukareru⟧: to get tired from weeding\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nA common household chore in Japan, especially during the humid summer months when weeds grow rapidly. School students are often assigned {草|くさ}むしり as a group activity on school grounds.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{草|くさ}{取|と}り→草取り：08533_kusatori⟧: weeding (alternative, slightly more casual term)\n- ⟦{除草|じょそう}→除草：18648_josou⟧: weeding (formal, includes chemical methods)\n- ⟦{雑草|ざっそう}→雑草：04996_zassou⟧: weeds (the plants themselves)\n- ⟦{草刈|くさか}り→草刈り：22813_kusakari⟧: mowing grass (uses tools, not pulling by hand)",
